   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization of the\ncounty of Tompkins to impose an additional one percent of sales and\ncompensating use taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S7804",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7804-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7804\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nof the county of Tompkins to impose an additional one percent of sales\nand compensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nto extend for two years Tompkins County's authorization to impose an\nadditional local 1% sales tax\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSec. 1 amends section 1210 of the tax law to change the sunset date from\n11/30/25 to 11/30/27\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe expiration of the additional 1% local sales tax would necessitate\napproximately $15 million's worth of reductions in County expenditures,\ncreating either a major impact on the availability of services or a 28%\nincrease in the county tax levy, or some combination thereof, as well as\nsubstantial sales tax revenue losses requiring spending reductions or\ntax increases for the City, towns and villages of Tompkins County. This\nbill extends the County's authorization to collect this 1% local sales\ntax, thereby preventing these potential negative impacts.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nnew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nrevenue raiser for Tompkins County\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nimmediately\n",
